CALCULATION CENTER – MULTI-SCENARIO READINESS (TABS) + WARNINGS CONFIRMATION
Angular + PrimeNG front end. Spring Boot back end only where noted.

SCOPE – READ FIRST
- Change ONLY the Readiness area of the calculation page, the scenario capsules' status
  look, and the "Run with warnings" confirmation dialog, as described below.
- Do NOT change: page layout, header, sidebar, breadcrumb, Switch to classic view pill,
  Reports card, Reset / Run calculation buttons and their positions, Execution stages
  (still shown only after Run), Result Aggregation / output table, History, persistence,
  APIs other than the fields listed under BACKEND, or any other workflow.
- REMOVE the current multi-scenario implementation where each scenario gets its own
  stacked/side-by-side readiness panel (one panel per scenario). Replace it with the
  single tabbed panel below. Also remove any toast/popup that says
  "all scenarios passed / some failed".
- Single scenario uses the SAME component (one tab). There must be one code path.

=====================================================================
1. STATE MODEL (per scenario)
=====================================================================
status: 'checking' | 'ready' | 'warning' | 'failed'
  - failed  = at least one criterion Failed
  - warning = no Failed, at least one Warning
  - ready   = all criteria Met
counts: met, warning, failed (out of 7 criteria from config/API)
checkedAt: timestamp

Overall (derived):
  checking  = any scenario 'checking'
  anyFailed = any scenario 'failed'
  readyCount = scenarios with 'ready' or 'warning'
  warnScenarios = scenarios with 'warning'
Keep the existing readiness API; call it per scenario (parallel) and update each tab as
its result arrives.

