Box behind the current step: #F3F6FA.

=====================================================================
5. READINESS PANEL (inside the Execution card, under the stepper)
=====================================================================
5a. Summary bar (text only)
- Full width, background #F7F9FB, no border, radius 8px, padding 10px 14px,
  3px left accent line (inset box-shadow): blue while checking, red if anyFailed,
  green otherwise. Margin-bottom 12px. Font 12.5px.
- Do NOT list scenario names, dots or spinners here (the tabs show them).
- Left text (bold part coloured blue/red/green, rest #4B5563 normal):
    checking:      **Checking readiness · <done> of <m> done**  Results appear in each tab
                   as they finish.
    anyFailed:     **<n> of <m> scenarios ready**  <x> not ready[ · <y> with warnings].
                   Open the red tab to see why.
    warnings only: **<m> of <m> scenarios ready**  <y> with warnings. You can run.
                   (1 scenario: **Ready**  <w> warnings. You can run.)
    all ready:     **<m> of <m> scenarios ready**  You can run the calculation.
                   (1 scenario: **Ready**  You can run the calculation.)
- Right side (only after checking finishes): "Checked <HH:mm>" (#6B7280, 11.5px) and an
  outlined "↻ Check again" button (height 28px, border #DDE2E9) that re-checks ALL
  selected scenarios.

5b. Tab bar
- White card (border #E6E9EE, radius 10px) containing the tab bar and the active tab body.
- Tab bar: white, bottom border #EEF1F5, horizontal padding 6px, scrolls horizontally
  if tabs overflow (no wrapping).
- One tab per selected scenario, in selection order. Tab: padding 12px 14px, 12.5px.
  Content: 16px status icon · scenario name (monospace, #1F2937) · short grey count text.
    checking  blue spinner icon · "Checking…"
    ready     green ✓ circle · "7/7 Met"
    warning   amber ! circle · "<n> warning(s)"
    failed    red ✕ circle · "<n> failed"
  Count text is plain #6B7280 text, NOT a coloured badge.
- Active tab: 2px #1D5FD6 bottom border (always blue, regardless of status).
- Default active tab when results are complete: first failed tab; else first warning
  tab; else first tab. While checking keep the first tab. User clicks switch tabs freely;
  do not auto-switch after the user has clicked a tab.

5c. Tab body – the 7 criteria of the active scenario
- Rows: padding 11px 18px, gap 14px, divider #F3F5F8.
- Left 16px icon: green ✓ Met · amber ! Warning · red ✕ Failed.
- Middle: criterion name 12.5px semibold #1F2937; message under it 12px normal #6B7280
  (backend message, e.g. account numbers / last run date).
- Right: status as plain coloured text with a small dot: "Met" green, "Warning" amber,
  "Failed" red. No pill backgrounds, no row background colour, no right-side spinners.
- While that scenario is checking: grey criterion names + a grey skeleton bar per row,
  nothing on the right.
- Criteria order and texts come from config/API (no hard-coding).

5d. Adding / removing scenarios
- Add a scenario → new tab appears in 'checking'; check ONLY that scenario.
- Remove a capsule → remove its tab immediately and re-evaluate summary, hint, stepper,
  header tag and Run button WITHOUT re-checking the others.
- Reset → existing behaviour (clears everything).

=====================================================================
6. "RUN WITH WARNINGS?" CONFIRMATION (replaces the old unchanged-data dialog)
=====================================================================
When: user clicks Run calculation, nothing failed, and at least one scenario has warnings
(this includes "Data Changed Since Last Run"). If no warnings → run immediately, no dialog.
If anyFailed → Run is disabled, dialog never opens. One dialog per Run click, never one
per scenario or per warning.

Component: p-dialog (modal) or p-confirmDialog with custom template.
- Width 620px (max 92vw), radius 14px, shadow 0 30px 70px -20px rgba(15,31,61,.45).
- Mask rgba(15,31,61,.32) with backdrop-filter: blur(1.5px).
- Header: padding 16px 20px; amber "!" circle icon (28px, bg #FFF3DE, text #8A4B00) +
  title "Run with warnings?" (15px semibold) + close ✕; background
  linear-gradient(90deg,#FFF6E5,#FFFFFF); bottom border #F6E3BF.
- Body padding 14px 18px.

Body content:
- Intro line (13px):
    1 scenario:  "<scenario> has <n> warning(s). Review before running."
    2+:          "<k> of <m> scenarios have warnings (<total> in total). Review them
                 before running."
- 1 scenario: list the warnings directly in one white bordered box (no scenario header).
- 2+ scenarios: small uppercase label "WARNINGS BY SCENARIO" (11px, #6B7280); if 3 or
  more groups also show "Expand all · Collapse all" links on the right.
  One group per scenario WITH warnings:
    group box: white, border #EEF1F5, radius 10px, margin-bottom 8px
    group header: white, bottom divider #F3F5F8, padding 9px 12px:
      chevron ▾/▸ · scenario name (monospace) · amber tag "<n> warning(s)"
    rows: padding 10px 12px, amber ! icon, warning name (12.5px semibold),
      message under it (12px, #6B7280) – include last run date/time and Run ID for
      "Data Changed Since Last Run".
  First 2 groups expanded, the rest collapsed.
  List area max-height ~330px with its own scroll; the dialog never exceeds the screen.
- Scenarios without warnings: one line "✓ <n> scenario(s) with no warnings: <names>"
  (green ✓, 12px, #4B5563).
- Acknowledgement (required) in a #F7F9FB box, radius 8px, padding 10px 12px:
    1 scenario: "I understand and want to run with these warnings."
    2+:         "I have reviewed the warnings for <k> scenario(s) and want to run."
- Footer: white, top border #EEF1F5, right aligned, padding 12px 18px:
    "Cancel" (outlined grey) – closes, nothing changes.
    Primary: "Run anyway" (1 scenario) / "Run anyway · <m> scenarios" (counts ALL
    selected scenarios that will run). Disabled until the checkbox is ticked.
    Checkbox resets to unticked each time the dialog opens.
- Esc / ✕ = Cancel. Focus starts on Cancel. Keyboard accessible.

